"notes": ["Source: Broncos 2026 media guide, regular-season 'INDIVIDUAL RECORDS' section (pdf pp. 803-817; printed page numbers equal pdf page numbers). Each stat has a Career, a Season and a Game list; most print ten rows or more (a tie prints the number once above the tied names); every printed named row of the needed lists is transcribed unless its scope_note says otherwise. Postseason records (pp. 844-850), opponent records and team records were not used.","through_season 2025: the credits page says the guide is current as of August 21, 2026, and the lists include 2025-season entries (Bo Nix 2025, Nik Bonitto 2025, RJ Harvey 2025 in the rookie lists).","Method: every row was read from 200-300 dpi crops of the page pictures and then every list was read a second time at 300 dpi against the transcription (all rows agreed). The IA OCR was used only as a cross-check and is unreliable here (it read Mike Anderson's 3,822 as 3.909, Brandon Marshall's 1,325 as 1,825, digits dropped in several other rows), so no value rests on the OCR. The p802 tackles column was checked against the year labels printed in the same table.","Ranks: the guide prints no rank numbers, only the value above a group of tied names. rank = competition rank by position (1,2,2,2,5...), tie = true on every member of a tied group. For tie-group continuation rows (value printed once above the group) raw shows the group value in square brackets, e.g. '[71] Brian Griese, 1998-2002'; for rows whose group continues across a column break (Von Miller, 2014 at 14.0 in the sacks list) the value is likewise inherited. A leading * on a value marks an NFL record in the guide (kept only in raw).","Game rows: the guide prints only a surname or initial+surname (e.g. 'Plummer', 'M. Anderson', 'D. Thomas'); `name` is as printed, `years` holds the date plus 'at/vs. opponent' moved in front of the printed order, and raw keeps the full printed line including (OT) and score notes.","PRINTING ANOMALIES kept as printed and flagged uncertain: (1) Career Receiving Yards prints Ed McCaffrey 6,200 above Courtland Sutton 6,357 (value rises at rank 6; this is the validator warning); (2) Season Receiving Yards prints 'Demaryius Thomas, 2014' twice (1,619 in 1st and 1,404 in 6th), the second is probably a typo for another player. Also two year spans differ between lists: Jon Keyworth is printed 1974-80 in the rushing-yards list but 1973-80 in the rushing-touchdowns list, and Riley Odoms 1972-83 in the receptions and receiving-yards lists but 1972-81 in the receiving-touchdowns list (each kept as printed).","Lists that run across a page or column break: season rush_yds (7 rows pdf p804 + 3 rows p805), season rec_yds (6 rows p809 + 4 rows p810), season sacks (5 rows at the bottom of the left column + 6 rows at the top of the right column of p816), game pass_yds (last two rows at the top of the right column of p806). pdf_page is the page where the list starts.","Not transcribed (count lines, not player rows): game rush_td rank 3 ('14 times'), game rec_td rank 2 ('16 times'), game pass_td rank 7 ('40 times'), season int rank 7 ('Five times'), game int rank 4 ('75 times'). Rookie-only lists, consecutive-game lists and average lists were not used.","Tackles: the guide has no career or single-game tackles list. The only tackle numbers are the year-by-year team leaders (pdf p802), so season/tackles is a `column` list of that table (29 of 57 seasons, 130+ tackles); the highest value there (Gradishar 286 in 1978, printed in bold) is the club single-season high only if no non-leader outdid it, which cannot be checked from the guide."]
}
